## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of closures, Promise deduplication, request cancellation, and caching strategies in building a production-ready fetch helper. It also touches on memory management with LRU caches and handling abortable requests.

## Key Concepts
- Closures for per-key state isolation
- Promise deduplication to prevent redundant network requests
- Cancellation with AbortController for stale requests
- LRU cache implementation using Map for ordered storage
- Edge cases: rapid toggling between keys and stale data handling

## Code Example
```javascript
const api = (() => {
  const inFlight = new Map();
  const cache = new Map();
  const MAX_CACHE = 50;

  function memoFetch(key, options = {}) {
    if (cache.has(key)) {
      const entry = cache.get(key);
      cache.delete(key);
      cache.set(key, entry);
      return Promise.resolve(entry);
    }

    if (inFlight.has(key)) {
      return inFlight.get(key);
    }

    const controller = new AbortController();
    const promise = fetch(key, { ...options, signal: controller.signal })
      .then(res => res.json())
      .then(data => {
        inFlight.delete(key);
        if (cache.size >= MAX_CACHE) {
          const firstKey = cache.keys().next().value;
          cache.delete(firstKey);
        }
        cache.set(key, data);
        return data;
      })
      .catch(err => {
        inFlight.delete(key);
        throw err;
      });

    inFlight.set(key, { promise, controller });
    return promise;
  }

  function cancel(key) {
    if (inFlight.has(key)) {
      inFlight.get(key).controller.abort();
      inFlight.delete(key);
    }
  }

  return { memoFetch, cancel };
})();
```

## Purpose

This question evaluates the ability to build a Redux-like state management solution using React's built-in hooks, demonstrate understanding of memoization patterns, and implement proper cleanup in side effects.

## Key Concepts

- **useReducer + Context**: Creating a centralized store with dispatch actions
- **Immutability**: Properly updating nested state without mutation
- **useMemo**: Computing derived data efficiently without unnecessary recalculations
- **React.memo**: Preventing unnecessary re-renders of list items
- **Debounced input**: Managing search input with delayed dispatch
- **Effect cleanup**: Properly handling unmount and dependency changes

## Code Example

```javascript
// ChatContext.js
const ChatContext = createContext();

const chatReducer = (state, action) => {
  switch (action.type) {
    case 'ADD_MESSAGE':
      return state.map(conv =>
        conv.id === action.payload.conversationId
          ? { ...conv, messages: [...conv.messages, action.payload.text], unread: conv.unread + 1 }
          : conv
      );
    case 'MARK_READ':
      return state.map(conv =>
        conv.id === action.payload.conversationId
          ? { ...conv, unread: 0 }
          : conv
      );
    default:
      return state;
  }
};

export const ChatProvider = ({ children }) => {
  const [conversations, dispatch] = useReducer(chatReducer, initialState);
  return (
    <ChatContext.Provider value={{ conversations, dispatch }}>
      {children}
    </ChatContext.Provider>
  );
};

// DebouncedSearchInput.jsx
const DebouncedSearchInput = ({ onFilter }) => {
  const [query, setQuery] = useState('');

  useEffect(() => {
    const timer = setTimeout(() => onFilter(query), 250);
    return () => clearTimeout(timer);
  }, [query, onFilter]);

  return <input value={query} onChange={e => setQuery(e.target.value)} />;
};

// useMemo selector
export const useUnreadCounts = (conversations) => {
  return useMemo(() => {
    const perConversation = conversations.reduce((acc, conv) => {
      acc[conv.id] = conv.unread;
      return acc;
    }, {});
    const total = conversations.reduce((sum, conv) => sum + conv.unread, 0);
    return { perConversation, total };
  }, [conversations]);
};

// Row.jsx (memoized)
const Row = React.memo(({ conversation, onMarkRead }) => (
  <div onClick={() => onMarkRead(conversation.id)}>
    {conversation.title} ({conversation.unread})
  </div>
));
```

